1
00:00:52,511 --> 00:00:53,387
ALL PERSONS, LOCATIONS, RELIGIONS,
INCIDENTS, AND ORGANIZATIONS IN THIS DRAMA

2
00:00:53,512 --> 00:00:54,346
ARE FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:54,472 --> 00:00:55,306
CHILD ACTORS HAVE FILMED SAFELY
UNDER PARENTAL SUPERVISION

4
00:00:55,431 --> 00:00:56,265
SCENES INVOLVING ANIMALS WERE FILMED
SAFELY WITH EXPERT ADVICE AND COOPERATION

5
00:01:20,539 --> 00:01:23,417
I just broke up with Han Tae-seung
and came straight here.

6
00:01:25,377 --> 00:01:27,213
I broke up with Park Su-a, too.

7
00:01:32,593 --> 00:01:33,844
You know, right?

8
00:01:35,846 --> 00:01:38,766
That we can never go back to how we were,

9
00:01:40,935 --> 00:01:42,728
and that this is the end.

10
00:01:44,980 --> 00:01:46,398
It's not your fault.

11
00:01:48,526 --> 00:01:50,778
Wherever this was headed,

12
00:01:51,487 --> 00:01:53,447
I insisted on seeing it through.

13
00:01:57,076 --> 00:02:00,329
Even if things got completely ruined…

14
00:02:03,499 --> 00:02:05,668
I wanted to see it through to the end.

15
00:02:08,963 --> 00:02:11,173
I don't think it was all bad.

16
00:02:14,468 --> 00:02:15,553
That end.

17
00:02:17,263 --> 00:02:18,764
Our rock bottom.

18
00:02:21,892 --> 00:02:24,395
Because now I know for sure…

19
00:02:27,147 --> 00:02:30,818
how terribly and agonizingly…

20
00:02:32,403 --> 00:02:34,113
we care about each other.

21
00:02:37,032 --> 00:02:39,994
I want to hurt you and ruin you more,

22
00:02:40,703 --> 00:02:41,954
but I just can't.

23
00:02:43,455 --> 00:02:44,790
It's so annoying.

24
00:02:49,420 --> 00:02:50,629
I know.

25
00:02:54,174 --> 00:02:55,259
It really is.

26
00:02:58,721 --> 00:03:00,514
Why are we such a mess?

27
00:03:01,181 --> 00:03:02,182
What can we do?

28
00:03:05,561 --> 00:03:07,021
It's just who we are.

29
00:03:29,460 --> 00:03:30,794
Let's break up,

30
00:03:31,879 --> 00:03:32,922
Namgung.

31
00:03:35,424 --> 00:03:36,550
Okay.

32
00:03:40,804 --> 00:03:42,306
Let's break up.

33
00:03:46,894 --> 00:03:47,895
Let's break up,

34
00:03:49,355 --> 00:03:50,230
Mi-do.

35
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:11,961
14. WHAT BROUGHT US TOGETHER?

36
00:04:49,957 --> 00:04:51,792
Namgung did nothing wrong.

37
00:04:54,169 --> 00:04:57,631
I fell for another man,
and that's why we broke up.

38
00:05:01,135 --> 00:05:03,053
So, Mom, just treat him like before--

39
00:05:03,178 --> 00:05:05,848
I've never seen Hoya cry like that.

40
00:05:08,225 --> 00:05:10,936
He was crying his heart out.

41
00:05:11,061 --> 00:05:15,024
He cried for hours on end
without saying a word before leaving.

42
00:05:16,567 --> 00:05:19,987
I don't know what happened
or why you two broke up.

43
00:05:20,612 --> 00:05:21,488
But

44
00:05:22,156 --> 00:05:24,533
I know you'll never get back together.

45
00:05:24,658 --> 00:05:26,910
I can feel it in my old bones.

46
00:05:28,912 --> 00:05:30,164
As for me,

47
00:05:30,873 --> 00:05:35,294
I can hardly remember
your dad's face these days.

48
00:05:37,629 --> 00:05:41,592
When I see his photos, I think,
“Oh, that's what he looked like.”

49
00:05:42,509 --> 00:05:44,344
“That's how he smiled.”

50
00:05:44,470 --> 00:05:46,805
It stings a little inside.

51
00:05:47,514 --> 00:05:50,476
But that's it.

52
00:05:53,771 --> 00:05:55,397
As life goes on,

53
00:05:56,607 --> 00:06:00,277
it gets so busy that it all fades.

54
00:06:01,570 --> 00:06:03,072
It all just disappears.

55
00:06:04,615 --> 00:06:08,285
You wonder how it's even possible.

56
00:06:09,995 --> 00:06:14,124
Then comes a day when that feels so sad.

57
00:06:15,626 --> 00:06:17,503
It will be the same for you two.

58
00:06:18,587 --> 00:06:23,300
So don't hate or resent him.

59
00:06:23,425 --> 00:06:25,803
And don't struggle so hard to forget him.

60
00:06:27,012 --> 00:06:29,098
Just let it flow.

61
00:06:30,349 --> 00:06:32,017
If you let it,

62
00:06:34,144 --> 00:06:35,604
you'll be able to live on.

63
00:06:38,273 --> 00:06:39,858
Life will continue.

64
00:06:50,410 --> 00:06:53,205
BORA BORA ROOM

65
00:06:53,330 --> 00:06:55,874
HONDURAS

66
00:07:24,153 --> 00:07:27,489
Sorry, I didn't think
it'd take you so long to find it.

67
00:07:32,327 --> 00:07:36,081
I thought that once I died,

68
00:07:36,206 --> 00:07:38,750
you'd get rid of this place right away.

69
00:07:41,170 --> 00:07:42,421
I could never do that.

70
00:07:44,298 --> 00:07:47,926
Honduras Karaoke is the only thing
you left behind for me.

71
00:07:49,136 --> 00:07:50,971
How could I ever leave this place?

72
00:07:58,228 --> 00:07:59,229
Bo-ra.

73
00:08:00,105 --> 00:08:01,231
Yes?

74
00:08:01,356 --> 00:08:02,566
I…

75
00:08:05,485 --> 00:08:07,487
I really loved you, you know?

76
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:12,159
It's true I was exhausted,

77
00:08:13,327 --> 00:08:16,038
and I hurt you because of that.

78
00:08:18,707 --> 00:08:20,000
But even so,

79
00:08:23,170 --> 00:08:25,005
I really loved you.

80
00:08:28,258 --> 00:08:29,134
I know.

81
00:08:31,011 --> 00:08:32,304
You do?

82
00:08:42,314 --> 00:08:43,482
Wan-do.

83
00:08:44,691 --> 00:08:45,525
Yes?

84
00:08:47,694 --> 00:08:49,738
Do you remember how we promised

85
00:08:50,405 --> 00:08:52,532
to go to the beach in Bora Bora together?

86
00:08:54,993 --> 00:08:55,911
Yes.

87
00:08:56,036 --> 00:08:58,121
I want to go there.

88
00:09:05,587 --> 00:09:07,256
Can you take me there?

89
00:09:28,193 --> 00:09:29,695
These don't look good either.

90
00:09:30,445 --> 00:09:32,906
Flashy things don't suit me anymore.

91
00:09:34,908 --> 00:09:35,826
Of course they do.

92
00:09:36,451 --> 00:09:38,662
You look gorgeous, Mom.

93
00:09:39,371 --> 00:09:40,414
You look insane.

94
00:09:44,376 --> 00:09:46,128
Dad made me do it.

95
00:09:46,253 --> 00:09:48,255
To say you're pretty 12 times,

96
00:09:48,380 --> 00:09:50,549
and that you look
younger than TA Jang five times.

97
00:09:50,674 --> 00:09:53,051
I'll tell Dad you were here for an hour.

98
00:09:56,179 --> 00:09:58,098
What? Do you have something to say?

99
00:10:00,559 --> 00:10:01,393
Need some cash?

100
00:10:01,518 --> 00:10:02,644
No.

101
00:10:04,354 --> 00:10:06,064
I won't call TA Jang "Dad."

102
00:10:06,189 --> 00:10:08,442
I didn't expect you to.

103
00:10:09,318 --> 00:10:10,485
Congratulations, Mom.

104
00:10:11,903 --> 00:10:14,239
Dad might need time to truly mean it.

105
00:10:15,198 --> 00:10:16,658
But I mean it.

106
00:10:17,784 --> 00:10:19,328
Try to understand Dad.

107
00:10:20,704 --> 00:10:21,580
Okay.

108
00:10:29,588 --> 00:10:31,506
He really kept that one promise.

109
00:10:42,601 --> 00:10:44,394
That's a good boy.

110
00:10:45,354 --> 00:10:48,106
I said we should get ox bone soup.
Sang-su likes rice.

111
00:10:49,358 --> 00:10:50,400
Is it good?

112
00:10:50,525 --> 00:10:51,526
Here, another bite.

113
00:10:56,656 --> 00:10:58,367
I like burgers.

114
00:10:58,492 --> 00:10:59,451
Here.

115
00:10:59,576 --> 00:11:01,453
Is it good?

116
00:11:01,578 --> 00:11:02,496
No ketchup?

117
00:11:03,580 --> 00:11:04,414
Oh, I forgot.

118
00:11:05,332 --> 00:11:07,834
It's bad for him anyway. Just eat.

119
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:20,180
Please reconsider.

120
00:11:20,764 --> 00:11:21,723
Just one last time.

121
00:11:21,848 --> 00:11:22,682
SEOUL FAMILY COURT

122
00:11:22,808 --> 00:11:26,269
I just feel so bad for Sang-su.

123
00:11:27,062 --> 00:11:30,941
Even if you won't be my wife,
can't you stay as Sang-su's mom?

124
00:11:31,066 --> 00:11:32,692
Please, I'm begging you.

125
00:11:36,029 --> 00:11:36,988
You…

126
00:11:38,824 --> 00:11:40,575
don't really need me.

127
00:11:50,794 --> 00:11:52,421
Never let him find out.

128
00:11:54,131 --> 00:11:56,591
You were so pathetic back then.

129
00:11:58,927 --> 00:12:00,846
So utterly pathetic.

130
00:12:11,273 --> 00:12:15,068
YEONHWARU

131
00:12:18,530 --> 00:12:19,698
Excuse me.

132
00:12:24,828 --> 00:12:26,371
It's my first time here.

133
00:12:27,414 --> 00:12:28,957
What's their signature dish?

134
00:12:53,106 --> 00:12:56,193
NAMGUNG, MI-DO
YEONHWARU

135
00:13:10,790 --> 00:13:15,712
TWO YEARS LATER

136
00:13:17,797 --> 00:13:23,011
I NEVER RESIGNED
BY EOM HO-SIK

137
00:13:30,644 --> 00:13:31,686
Thank you.

138
00:13:48,370 --> 00:13:50,956
HO-SIK'S PICK

139
00:13:53,625 --> 00:13:56,169
Executive Director Yoon
is up to something.

140
00:13:56,294 --> 00:13:58,505
He's been calling in
the executives privately,

141
00:13:59,339 --> 00:14:02,509
and now he's eyeing a restructuring.

142
00:14:03,843 --> 00:14:07,889
I need you to take over that team
as Team Leader.

143
00:14:08,014 --> 00:14:09,349
A 20% raise.

144
00:14:09,474 --> 00:14:10,392
What?

145
00:14:10,517 --> 00:14:13,228
And a separate contract for incentive pay

146
00:14:13,353 --> 00:14:15,730
of up to 20% of my salary
if the project KPIs are met.

147
00:14:15,855 --> 00:14:17,941
Then I'll give it some thought.

148
00:14:18,066 --> 00:14:19,943
Like hell you will, damn it!

149
00:14:20,068 --> 00:14:22,612
I'm being ground down at work
because of you!

150
00:14:22,737 --> 00:14:25,031
If only you hadn't posted that video.

151
00:14:25,156 --> 00:14:26,533
Jeez, seriously.

152
00:14:28,034 --> 00:14:28,868
Did you see this?

153
00:14:30,412 --> 00:14:31,496
Look.

154
00:14:32,038 --> 00:14:32,872
What's this?

155
00:14:34,374 --> 00:14:35,750
SWEET POTATO SWAP

156
00:14:35,875 --> 00:14:37,711
Wait, hold on.

157
00:14:38,378 --> 00:14:39,421
Is that our manager?

158
00:14:40,088 --> 00:14:41,590
-It is, right?
-Yes, it's him.

159
00:14:41,715 --> 00:14:43,341
Right? That's Manager Eom!

160
00:14:43,466 --> 00:14:44,884
-It is.
-See? Told you!

161
00:14:45,468 --> 00:14:47,053
-Hey, this fell.
-Yes, sir.

162
00:14:47,178 --> 00:14:49,848
SWEET POTATOES

163
00:14:51,224 --> 00:14:52,976
Please don't damage them.

164
00:14:56,229 --> 00:14:57,856
HM CONFECTIONERY EXPOSED!

165
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:01,818
OVER 5 MILLION VIEWS

166
00:15:02,152 --> 00:15:03,236
HERO EOM HO-SIK
TRUE MENTOR EOM

167
00:15:03,361 --> 00:15:04,321
I LOVE HIM
HE'S OUR HOPE

168
00:15:04,446 --> 00:15:06,072
I NEVER RESIGNED
BY EOM HO-SIK

169
00:15:06,573 --> 00:15:08,158
TRULY INSPIRING
A PAGE-TURNER

170
00:15:08,325 --> 00:15:09,868
SWEET, SPICY, AND ADDICTIVE

171
00:15:10,535 --> 00:15:11,995
EOM HO-SIK APPOINTED AS DIRECTOR

172
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:15,206
Hey, this isn't the life I wanted.

173
00:15:15,332 --> 00:15:17,459
I just wanted to go to Tongyeong,

174
00:15:17,584 --> 00:15:19,628
collect my paychecks, and coast by.

175
00:15:19,753 --> 00:15:21,338
Now look at this mess.

176
00:15:21,463 --> 00:15:23,465
I'm caught in this bloody power struggle!

177
00:15:23,590 --> 00:15:26,760
God, it's suffocating. Damn it.

178
00:15:27,594 --> 00:15:31,139
I never wanted
to climb this high, you hear me?

179
00:15:31,264 --> 00:15:32,140
Eom the Great.

180
00:15:33,099 --> 00:15:34,643
Why are you acting so weak?

181
00:15:34,768 --> 00:15:36,478
Gen Z will be disappointed.

182
00:15:36,603 --> 00:15:38,438
To hell with that, damn it.

183
00:15:38,563 --> 00:15:40,815
I'm not getting ground down alone.
You are, too!

184
00:15:40,940 --> 00:15:43,443
We're both on the grater.
We're meant to get ground down.

185
00:15:43,568 --> 00:15:44,527
Come back to work now!

186
00:15:44,653 --> 00:15:46,363
Let's talk salary first.

187
00:15:46,488 --> 00:15:47,322
Salary?

188
00:15:56,039 --> 00:15:57,082
Senior Associate Park.

189
00:15:58,541 --> 00:16:01,044
Right, Manager Gung

190
00:16:01,169 --> 00:16:04,339
will start working
at headquarters next week.

191
00:16:06,549 --> 00:16:09,552
You two haven't seen each other
in about two years, right?

192
00:16:11,971 --> 00:16:14,307
Long time no see, Associate Park.

193
00:16:16,059 --> 00:16:16,976
Or should I say…

194
00:16:18,728 --> 00:16:20,146
Senior Associate Park?

195
00:16:24,818 --> 00:16:26,027
For the Maison Project,

196
00:16:26,861 --> 00:16:28,822
you rejected the vendor we found.

197
00:16:28,947 --> 00:16:30,240
May I ask why?

198
00:16:30,365 --> 00:16:33,868
Oh, that pastry chef,
Louis Maltese or whatever?

199
00:16:33,993 --> 00:16:35,453
It's Pastry Chef Louis Martin.

200
00:16:36,204 --> 00:16:37,997
The top pastry chef in Paris.

201
00:16:38,957 --> 00:16:41,668
We worked had to contact him
and just needed sign-off.

202
00:16:41,793 --> 00:16:43,002
Why did you reject it?

203
00:16:43,128 --> 00:16:44,671
I didn't like his face.

204
00:16:44,796 --> 00:16:45,839
Wow.

205
00:16:48,550 --> 00:16:49,676
I'm just kidding.

206
00:16:51,511 --> 00:16:53,805
Come to my welcome party to find out.

207
00:17:03,565 --> 00:17:06,484
I can't make it today.
I have a blind date.

208
00:17:06,609 --> 00:17:07,819
I didn't ask.

209
00:17:09,112 --> 00:17:10,029
Senior Associate Park.

210
00:17:10,155 --> 00:17:13,616
In situations like this,
just say you have personal plans.

211
00:17:13,742 --> 00:17:16,953
You got promoted a while ago,
but you still lack tact.

212
00:17:17,620 --> 00:17:21,207
I'll hear your reasons in person
when you come in next week.

213
00:17:32,469 --> 00:17:33,303
PROSECUTION

214
00:17:33,428 --> 00:17:36,389
Defendant Sim Hae-ju is a repeat offender,

215
00:17:37,390 --> 00:17:40,560
who has engaged in illegal hacking
since his teens.

216
00:17:42,228 --> 00:17:44,439
The defendant is not a mere hacker.

217
00:17:44,564 --> 00:17:45,398
THE WORST WOMAN

218
00:17:45,523 --> 00:17:46,983
Per the client's request,

219
00:17:47,108 --> 00:17:49,068
he illegally obtained and shared data…

220
00:17:49,194 --> 00:17:50,653
Get ready to cry.

221
00:17:50,779 --> 00:17:51,863
…as a data broker.

222
00:17:51,988 --> 00:17:52,947
DEFENSE, DEFENDANT

223
00:17:53,072 --> 00:17:54,949
Should a defense lawyer say that?

224
00:17:55,074 --> 00:17:57,577
For six months off your sentence,
you better cry.

225
00:17:58,411 --> 00:18:00,538
A single tear gets you six months off.

226
00:18:00,663 --> 00:18:03,333
Bawling your eyes out gets you a year off.

227
00:18:03,458 --> 00:18:06,669
-Why did you even take my case?
-…even fully aware of the facts…

228
00:18:06,795 --> 00:18:09,130
You knew who I was from the start, right?

229
00:18:10,089 --> 00:18:10,924
Please continue.

230
00:18:11,049 --> 00:18:12,675
In particular, the defendant

231
00:18:12,801 --> 00:18:15,595
obtained targets' identities
and daily routines…

232
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:18,139
The woman I like told me to be good.

233
00:18:18,264 --> 00:18:20,809
So I do pro bono work now and then.

234
00:18:22,143 --> 00:18:23,728
And you looked so pathetic.

235
00:18:24,646 --> 00:18:25,730
So why not?

236
00:18:25,855 --> 00:18:27,482
…securing private records

237
00:18:27,607 --> 00:18:29,526
and delivering them to the client.

238
00:18:30,276 --> 00:18:31,486
He's wrapping it up.

239
00:18:31,611 --> 00:18:32,612
Start crying now.

240
00:18:38,368 --> 00:18:40,453
Think about when your grandma passed away.

241
00:18:40,578 --> 00:18:41,663
Watch it.

242
00:18:41,788 --> 00:18:43,248
Or back in middle school,

243
00:18:44,791 --> 00:18:46,000
when you got expelled.

244
00:18:47,669 --> 00:18:49,963
You used to live at Seoul Station.

245
00:18:50,797 --> 00:18:51,631
Yes.

246
00:18:52,298 --> 00:18:53,842
It's not a big deal.

247
00:18:55,635 --> 00:18:58,096
If I had met you back then…

248
00:19:02,559 --> 00:19:05,520
I'd have made sure
you weren't unfairly expelled,

249
00:19:06,646 --> 00:19:08,690
and I'd given your grandmother
a proper funeral

250
00:19:08,815 --> 00:19:11,067
instead of a funeral
for an unclaimed body.

251
00:19:13,570 --> 00:19:16,155
And you wouldn't
have gotten beaten to a pulp

252
00:19:16,823 --> 00:19:18,741
-Prosecutor, has he…
-…by homeless guys.

253
00:19:18,867 --> 00:19:20,660
…reached a settlement with the victim?

254
00:19:20,785 --> 00:19:23,246
They haven't reached a settlement yet,

255
00:19:23,371 --> 00:19:26,332
and no restitution has been confirmed.

256
00:19:27,250 --> 00:19:28,126
Nice.

257
00:19:29,335 --> 00:19:30,628
Keep it up.

258
00:19:30,753 --> 00:19:33,840
…that the defendant
be sentenced to five years.

259
00:19:37,135 --> 00:19:39,846
Counsel, make your closing argument.

260
00:19:41,764 --> 00:19:44,350
The prosecution's claims are untrue.

261
00:19:44,475 --> 00:19:46,853
Where would you call cut here?

262
00:19:46,978 --> 00:19:48,187
FILM DIRECTING

263
00:19:48,980 --> 00:19:49,981
The right answer

264
00:19:50,940 --> 00:19:51,816
doesn't exist.

265
00:19:52,567 --> 00:19:55,695
But you have to be able to explain
why you cut here.

266
00:19:57,322 --> 00:20:00,950
Directing isn't about right answers,
but about making reasoned choices

267
00:20:01,075 --> 00:20:04,203
and convincing people
of your choices to the end.

268
00:20:05,163 --> 00:20:07,165
Now, let's look at the next scene.

269
00:20:13,755 --> 00:20:14,714
KIMOON UNIVERSITY

270
00:20:14,839 --> 00:20:16,174
Good work, everyone.

271
00:20:19,928 --> 00:20:22,472
I didn't know if I should tell you,

272
00:20:23,139 --> 00:20:24,807
but you should probably know.

273
00:20:25,725 --> 00:20:27,060
Namgung came back to Korea.

274
00:20:27,602 --> 00:20:29,062
So,

275
00:20:29,187 --> 00:20:30,855
don't come home for a while.

276
00:20:30,980 --> 00:20:33,024
What if he doesn't visit because of you?

277
00:20:34,442 --> 00:20:35,902
What is he even saying?

278
00:20:36,027 --> 00:20:38,863
Hey, did you hear
what happened in the equipment room?

279
00:20:39,781 --> 00:20:40,990
Is it true?

280
00:20:41,115 --> 00:20:43,368
They said an FX7 got totally wrecked.

281
00:20:43,493 --> 00:20:46,037
Isn't that at least ten million won?

282
00:20:46,162 --> 00:20:48,498
The department chair is desperate
to catch who did it.

283
00:20:48,623 --> 00:20:52,543
Apparently, the security cameras
on that floor and throughout the building

284
00:20:52,669 --> 00:20:54,295
were down at that exact moment.

285
00:20:54,420 --> 00:20:55,588
But TA Baek said

286
00:20:55,713 --> 00:20:59,342
they saw a man and a woman
go in there right at that time.

287
00:21:00,259 --> 00:21:01,511
Clearly outsiders.

288
00:21:01,636 --> 00:21:03,221
Wait, both of them in there?

289
00:21:03,346 --> 00:21:04,389
Yes.

290
00:21:04,514 --> 00:21:06,474
Damn, what were they doing in there?

291
00:21:06,599 --> 00:21:07,934
What else? It's obvious.

292
00:21:08,059 --> 00:21:10,228
-That's crazy.
-Whatever, let's get coffee.

293
00:21:16,985 --> 00:21:19,946
FILM EQUIPMENT ROOM

294
00:21:39,340 --> 00:21:40,383
Looking for this?

295
00:21:42,010 --> 00:21:44,470
What? How'd you get in here?

296
00:21:45,930 --> 00:21:47,265
Same way as last time?

297
00:21:51,477 --> 00:21:52,645
Just kidding.

298
00:21:55,273 --> 00:21:56,607
I have two card cases.

299
00:21:58,568 --> 00:22:00,820
What? So you didn't find it?

300
00:22:01,738 --> 00:22:02,905
No.

301
00:22:05,283 --> 00:22:07,994
Mine wasn't the only card in there.
Don't worry.

302
00:22:08,119 --> 00:22:09,704
I took care of the cameras, too.

303
00:22:09,829 --> 00:22:11,539
Still, just in case--

304
00:22:11,664 --> 00:22:12,832
I heard Namgung Ho

305
00:22:13,875 --> 00:22:15,418
is back in Korea.

306
00:22:20,506 --> 00:22:21,716
So you already knew.

307
00:22:25,887 --> 00:22:28,598
-You went back to my mom?
-For a root touch-up.

308
00:22:28,723 --> 00:22:31,100
Who gets their roots
touched up every week?

309
00:22:31,225 --> 00:22:34,145
Forget it. Don't go there anymore.

310
00:22:34,270 --> 00:22:35,229
I'm warning you.

311
00:22:35,354 --> 00:22:36,355
Why not?

312
00:22:37,273 --> 00:22:39,233
Worried I'll run into Namgung Ho?

313
00:22:46,991 --> 00:22:48,201
Do you miss him?

314
00:22:53,915 --> 00:22:55,500
Do you miss Namgung Ho?

315
00:22:56,709 --> 00:22:57,794
Answer me.

316
00:23:05,009 --> 00:23:07,386
You sure you left it
in the equipment room?

317
00:23:07,512 --> 00:23:09,889
I don't remember,
but I was definitely in there.

318
00:23:10,014 --> 00:23:11,390
Wow, you don't remember?

319
00:23:11,516 --> 00:23:12,683
-Stop losing it.
-Seriously.

320
00:23:12,809 --> 00:23:14,519
-Jeez.
-Did you check inside?

321
00:23:14,644 --> 00:23:16,979
Here it is! I thought I lost it.

322
00:23:17,105 --> 00:23:18,314
-So clumsy.
-Cut it out.

323
00:23:18,439 --> 00:23:19,690
-Don't lose it.
-Come on.

324
00:23:19,816 --> 00:23:20,775
-Buy us coffee.
-Yes.

325
00:23:20,900 --> 00:23:22,443
-Sorry.
-Sweet!

326
00:23:31,869 --> 00:23:33,454
Were you playing with me?

327
00:23:36,249 --> 00:23:37,834
You can play with me.

328
00:23:38,876 --> 00:23:40,294
But only with me.

329
00:23:43,756 --> 00:23:46,134
Fine, I admit I was clingy.

330
00:23:47,176 --> 00:23:48,219
But you

331
00:23:49,345 --> 00:23:51,305
indulged me one out of ten times.

332
00:23:51,430 --> 00:23:53,057
You gave me hope.

333
00:23:53,599 --> 00:23:57,353
You didn't pull away just now either.
You made my heart race again.

334
00:24:09,448 --> 00:24:10,575
Tell me you don't.

335
00:24:13,244 --> 00:24:14,954
Tell me you don't miss

336
00:24:16,372 --> 00:24:17,832
Namgung Ho at all.

337
00:24:21,836 --> 00:24:24,005
Are you that insecure?

338
00:24:26,090 --> 00:24:28,676
Do you still think I'm playing with you?

339
00:24:33,181 --> 00:24:35,183
You asked if I miss Namgung Ho.

340
00:24:36,309 --> 00:24:38,561
Yes, I do miss him.

341
00:24:39,812 --> 00:24:41,814
But not in the way you think.

342
00:24:42,607 --> 00:24:44,066
I just

343
00:24:45,568 --> 00:24:47,653
wonder how he's doing.

344
00:24:48,487 --> 00:24:49,739
I'm worried about him.

345
00:24:52,491 --> 00:24:53,993
Also…

346
00:24:58,122 --> 00:25:01,292
it hurts so much to see you
getting hurt because of me.

347
00:25:03,461 --> 00:25:05,755
Seeing you suffer because of Namgung Ho

348
00:25:07,798 --> 00:25:09,258
breaks my heart.

349
00:25:13,095 --> 00:25:15,723
So I can't follow my heart
and fall for you.

350
00:25:25,149 --> 00:25:27,652
You think I'm hurting
because of Namgung Ho?

351
00:25:34,033 --> 00:25:35,117
No.

352
00:25:36,619 --> 00:25:38,537
It's because you
won't give me reassurance.

353
00:25:41,582 --> 00:25:42,541
Reassure me.

354
00:25:43,918 --> 00:25:45,711
If you don't want to hurt me,

355
00:25:47,129 --> 00:25:48,339
reassure me.

356
00:26:49,984 --> 00:26:51,485
How was your blind date?

357
00:27:19,263 --> 00:27:20,973
Can I ask you something?

358
00:27:21,849 --> 00:27:22,767
Go ahead.

359
00:27:22,892 --> 00:27:26,020
Why did you send me those plants?

360
00:27:26,854 --> 00:27:29,231
My transfer to headquarters
at the beginning of the year

361
00:27:29,357 --> 00:27:32,151
got canceled when they decided
the Maison Project

362
00:27:32,860 --> 00:27:34,487
would go with local collaboration.

363
00:27:35,571 --> 00:27:37,531
But I'd already shipped my things.

364
00:27:39,367 --> 00:27:42,620
And plant regulations are strict,
so I couldn't get them back.

365
00:27:42,745 --> 00:27:44,121
I cared about them,

366
00:27:45,456 --> 00:27:48,167
so I wondered who'd take
the best care of them,

367
00:27:49,210 --> 00:27:50,211
and chose you.

368
00:27:51,837 --> 00:27:52,671
That's a lie.

369
00:27:53,464 --> 00:27:54,548
You canceled

370
00:27:55,424 --> 00:27:56,884
your transfer yourself.

371
00:27:57,009 --> 00:27:58,803
The team had been assembled,

372
00:27:58,928 --> 00:28:01,097
but you canceled it unilaterally.

373
00:28:01,222 --> 00:28:03,015
Your assignment was originally six months,

374
00:28:03,140 --> 00:28:05,643
but you stayed two years
because you wanted to.

375
00:28:07,520 --> 00:28:08,938
It was because of Ms. Lee, right?

376
00:28:11,482 --> 00:28:13,567
You stayed away because of her,
didn't you?

377
00:28:17,488 --> 00:28:19,156
You think it was because of Lee Mi-do?

378
00:28:19,281 --> 00:28:21,242
-Was it not?
-No, it wasn't.

379
00:28:22,827 --> 00:28:24,537
I thought my feelings for you

380
00:28:25,746 --> 00:28:27,832
had to be at 100%.

381
00:28:29,542 --> 00:28:32,294
I thought I shouldn't return until then.

382
00:28:44,723 --> 00:28:46,392
Then what about now?

383
00:28:48,727 --> 00:28:50,187
Are they at 100% now?

384
00:28:52,815 --> 00:28:54,567
Is that why you came back?

385
00:28:57,153 --> 00:28:57,987
No.

386
00:29:02,158 --> 00:29:04,118
Because I couldn't bring them down to 0%.

387
00:29:07,955 --> 00:29:09,665
That's why I came back.

388
00:29:23,721 --> 00:29:25,264
Who was that woman?

389
00:29:25,389 --> 00:29:29,018
The one you were eating gelato with
in Le Marais back in April.

390
00:29:29,143 --> 00:29:31,687
Assistant Manager Oh in General Affairs
said they saw you.

391
00:29:31,812 --> 00:29:33,522
My neighbor, Juliette Laurent.

392
00:29:33,647 --> 00:29:34,940
What's between you two?

393
00:29:35,065 --> 00:29:36,484
We eat gelato together.

394
00:29:37,651 --> 00:29:41,822
For the record, her girlfriend
is our Paris Team Leader, Camille.

395
00:29:44,575 --> 00:29:46,410
-Anything else?
-No.

396
00:30:00,174 --> 00:30:03,010
Why did you suddenly reject
Martin, the pastry chef?

397
00:30:04,178 --> 00:30:05,221
Seriously, right now?

398
00:30:05,346 --> 00:30:06,514
Because  Lumière Homme

399
00:30:06,639 --> 00:30:09,517
named him one of the 100
most attractive men in their thirties,

400
00:30:10,768 --> 00:30:11,852
right?

401
00:30:13,479 --> 00:30:15,314
Not because of another issue.

402
00:30:15,439 --> 00:30:17,358
You just didn't want me working with him.

403
00:30:18,359 --> 00:30:19,318
You were jealous.

404
00:30:20,027 --> 00:30:21,445
Am I right?

405
00:30:28,410 --> 00:30:30,621
-Hey.
-Why did you kill it?

406
00:30:31,455 --> 00:30:33,832
The snake plant
I gave you before you left.

407
00:30:34,542 --> 00:30:36,210
Why did you kill just that one?

408
00:30:44,510 --> 00:30:45,719
Because of you.

409
00:30:46,595 --> 00:30:48,722
You said to water it when I missed you.

410
00:30:48,847 --> 00:30:51,100
So I kept watering it, and it died.

411
00:30:54,270 --> 00:30:55,980
Anything else you want to know?

412
00:30:57,481 --> 00:30:58,315
No.

413
00:30:58,440 --> 00:31:01,277
No, you said that earlier too.

414
00:31:01,402 --> 00:31:04,029
Think carefully. There might be more.

415
00:31:15,916 --> 00:31:17,209
I missed you.

416
00:31:19,795 --> 00:31:22,214
I missed you so, so much.

417
00:31:52,703 --> 00:31:54,788
Has it been six months already?

418
00:31:54,913 --> 00:31:57,333
Now that that punk Namgung is back,

419
00:31:57,458 --> 00:31:58,667
we can go float fishing.

420
00:31:58,792 --> 00:32:01,837
Great. I don't have
weekend classes this term.

421
00:32:01,962 --> 00:32:03,672
Oh, really? That's great, man.

422
00:32:04,632 --> 00:32:07,509
You two, take this food to Hoya.

423
00:32:09,178 --> 00:32:11,013
Why? He's coming tomorrow evening.

424
00:32:17,561 --> 00:32:20,022
-Hey.
-What did you just say?

425
00:32:20,147 --> 00:32:23,776
No calls, no texts,
and definitely no messaging.

426
00:32:25,569 --> 00:32:28,322
We only meet here once a year,
on Wan-do's birthday.

427
00:32:36,580 --> 00:32:38,874
From now on, let's meet once a year.

428
00:32:43,671 --> 00:32:46,507
BROTHER CLEANING

429
00:33:03,857 --> 00:33:05,818
This is about what happened, right?

430
00:33:06,944 --> 00:33:08,445
Because of what I said then.

431
00:33:10,489 --> 00:33:12,574
You know that's not why.

432
00:33:16,203 --> 00:33:19,498
Even if you set Mi-do aside,
what about Mom?

433
00:33:20,958 --> 00:33:22,668
What about Wan-do, your shadow?

434
00:33:24,837 --> 00:33:26,255
Don't you worry about us?

435
00:33:26,380 --> 00:33:27,673
No, I don't.

436
00:33:30,926 --> 00:33:32,803
Because I know you'll do fine.

437
00:33:35,389 --> 00:33:37,766
You'll look after them better than anyone.

438
00:33:39,768 --> 00:33:41,520
So I'm not worried at all.

439
00:33:55,451 --> 00:33:57,035
Of course, that's a given.

440
00:33:57,161 --> 00:33:59,747
I'm the eldest son
of our clan's 32nd generation.

441
00:34:00,581 --> 00:34:02,249
Who'll look after us if not me?

442
00:34:02,374 --> 00:34:03,959
Of course I'll look after us.

443
00:34:08,589 --> 00:34:10,048
I'll take care of you, too.

444
00:34:11,049 --> 00:34:11,925
Namgung Ho.

445
00:34:12,634 --> 00:34:14,511
I'll take care of you, too.

446
00:34:16,013 --> 00:34:19,099
Of course I will. You're my brother.

447
00:34:21,602 --> 00:34:24,313
Seeing you once a year
doesn't mean you're not my brother.

448
00:34:25,481 --> 00:34:29,359
Once a brother, always a brother.

449
00:34:30,736 --> 00:34:31,779
Got it?

450
00:34:33,947 --> 00:34:34,990
Got it?

451
00:34:37,493 --> 00:34:39,036
Say you got it.

452
00:34:45,667 --> 00:34:47,461
Why aren't you saying anything?

453
00:34:50,255 --> 00:34:51,632
Say something.

454
00:34:54,384 --> 00:34:56,595
Why won't you say anything?

455
00:35:23,038 --> 00:35:24,832
We'll still meet once a year.

456
00:35:24,957 --> 00:35:26,667
Don't be too upset.

457
00:35:29,753 --> 00:35:31,213
How are your classes going?

458
00:35:32,130 --> 00:35:33,257
Still lifting weights?

459
00:35:34,007 --> 00:35:35,008
Hey.

460
00:35:35,968 --> 00:35:37,886
People sometimes catch
nine-foot fish here.

461
00:35:41,515 --> 00:35:44,351
Is once every five years
really "sometimes"?

462
00:35:45,519 --> 00:35:47,145
It's just the owner's gimmick.

463
00:35:48,480 --> 00:35:49,898
If you release the nine-foot fish,

464
00:35:50,899 --> 00:35:52,442
it'll grant you a wish.

465
00:35:52,568 --> 00:35:53,986
It wouldn't change things.

466
00:35:54,820 --> 00:35:56,488
Even if you catch a giant fish,

467
00:35:56,613 --> 00:35:58,156
it'll be once a year.

468
00:35:59,032 --> 00:36:00,450
No more often than that.

469
00:36:02,286 --> 00:36:03,954
In the next life,

470
00:36:06,540 --> 00:36:08,625
I'll be born as your dad.

471
00:36:14,548 --> 00:36:16,049
I really will.

472
00:36:17,759 --> 00:36:18,969
In this life,

473
00:36:21,430 --> 00:36:23,223
we may part like this.

474
00:36:25,058 --> 00:36:26,393
But in the next one,

475
00:36:27,603 --> 00:36:29,813
I promise I'll be your dad.

476
00:36:31,899 --> 00:36:32,816
So that…

477
00:36:34,735 --> 00:36:36,570
I can repay everything…

478
00:36:39,031 --> 00:36:40,449
you've done for me,

479
00:36:42,951 --> 00:36:44,411
many times over.

480
00:37:02,346 --> 00:37:03,597
Ho.

481
00:37:14,524 --> 00:37:15,984
You'll do just fine.

482
00:37:19,655 --> 00:37:20,989
Even without us,

483
00:37:22,908 --> 00:37:24,493
you'll do really well.

484
00:37:29,122 --> 00:37:30,582
Thanks for everything.

485
00:38:40,944 --> 00:38:42,988
This wasn't a coincidence.

486
00:38:46,658 --> 00:38:49,119
I waited over two hours downstairs.

487
00:38:50,954 --> 00:38:53,582
Which means I could easily avoid you, too.

488
00:38:55,250 --> 00:38:56,918
Even if you visit my family,

489
00:38:58,170 --> 00:38:59,921
we'll never cross paths.

490
00:39:03,842 --> 00:39:05,427
I heard from Yeong-do.

491
00:39:05,552 --> 00:39:08,138
You said you'd see my family
only once a year?

492
00:39:11,475 --> 00:39:12,768
Don't bother.

493
00:39:13,810 --> 00:39:15,562
We were fine for two years.

494
00:39:17,355 --> 00:39:18,565
So let's just keep--

495
00:39:18,690 --> 00:39:19,775
I put it off.

496
00:39:23,195 --> 00:39:24,821
I need some time.

497
00:39:29,659 --> 00:39:32,412
I told my landlord
I'm not renewing the lease.

498
00:39:32,537 --> 00:39:34,706
I'll move out in a month,

499
00:39:35,791 --> 00:39:37,042
and I won't ever…

500
00:39:39,836 --> 00:39:42,047
see you again after tomorrow.

501
00:39:43,131 --> 00:39:44,174
Namgung…

502
00:39:45,342 --> 00:39:46,218
Mi-do.

503
00:39:49,679 --> 00:39:50,889
Let's go on a trip.

504
00:39:55,310 --> 00:39:58,063
There's a place
I really want to go with you.

505
00:40:17,415 --> 00:40:21,711
Gangnam Express Bus Terminal,
Platform 13, at 9:10 a.m. tomorrow.

506
00:40:22,504 --> 00:40:24,214
Don't come if you don't want to.

507
00:40:24,339 --> 00:40:27,592
But if you don't, this will be

508
00:40:28,301 --> 00:40:30,262
the last time we see each other.

509
00:41:51,676 --> 00:41:52,510
Mi-do.

510
00:41:54,262 --> 00:41:55,972
Let's make one promise today.

511
00:41:57,307 --> 00:41:58,600
Just for today,

512
00:41:59,267 --> 00:42:01,394
let's be completely honest, no lies.

513
00:42:02,687 --> 00:42:04,314
If either of us lies,

514
00:42:05,357 --> 00:42:07,567
a flick on the forehead. Deal?

515
00:42:08,944 --> 00:42:11,571
Sorry, but I've always been
honest with you.

516
00:42:13,698 --> 00:42:16,034
Why do you feel the need to say that?

517
00:42:19,454 --> 00:42:22,499
Did you go to Damyang with Gong Ji-seok
on my discharge day?

518
00:42:27,879 --> 00:42:28,713
No, I didn't.

519
00:42:29,422 --> 00:42:31,883
I had a field trip for my grad project--

520
00:42:39,599 --> 00:42:40,433
What about you?

521
00:42:40,558 --> 00:42:44,896
Where did you go on my 22nd birthday
after I dumped you?

522
00:42:45,939 --> 00:42:48,066
You went to Angela Cho's, didn't you?

523
00:42:48,191 --> 00:42:49,401
Not her place. A motel.

524
00:42:50,777 --> 00:42:52,237
We went to a motel.

525
00:42:54,698 --> 00:42:56,574
You sound awfully proud of that.

526
00:42:56,700 --> 00:42:58,493
We weren't dating back then,

527
00:42:58,618 --> 00:43:01,246
and I dated Angela Cho after that day.
What's the problem?

528
00:43:09,629 --> 00:43:10,880
Do you regret knowing me?

529
00:43:12,299 --> 00:43:14,342
Do you regret having me in your life?

530
00:43:21,308 --> 00:43:22,309
No.

531
00:43:22,434 --> 00:43:25,270
I've never regretted knowing you
for a single second.

532
00:43:27,731 --> 00:43:29,691
Because that day was an accident.

533
00:43:31,359 --> 00:43:33,570
It was truly an unavoidable accident.

534
00:43:34,946 --> 00:43:37,657
What about you? Do you regret knowing me?

535
00:43:37,782 --> 00:43:38,992
Yes, I do.

536
00:43:40,702 --> 00:43:42,495
I've always thought

537
00:43:42,620 --> 00:43:45,540
I was a curse
that brought the worst into your life.

538
00:43:45,665 --> 00:43:46,666
Namgung.

539
00:43:46,791 --> 00:43:50,086
If you and I had met like ordinary people,

540
00:43:52,005 --> 00:43:53,923
our ending would've been different.

541
00:43:55,091 --> 00:43:56,634
It makes me a little bitter.

542
00:44:06,227 --> 00:44:08,355
So that's why you brought me here.

543
00:44:08,480 --> 00:44:12,400
To say everything you wanted to say,
hear everything you needed to,

544
00:44:13,068 --> 00:44:14,402
and leave nothing behind.

545
00:44:16,905 --> 00:44:18,990
You won't see me after today?

546
00:44:20,909 --> 00:44:22,911
All right, let's do that.

547
00:44:24,371 --> 00:44:26,039
Let's just say goodbye here.

548
00:44:26,998 --> 00:44:28,208
Have a good life.

549
00:44:38,551 --> 00:44:41,930
VACANT

550
00:44:42,055 --> 00:44:43,598
GANGNEUNG, BEAUTIFUL ALL YEAR

551
00:44:43,723 --> 00:44:45,058
To the terminal, please.

552
00:45:00,698 --> 00:45:02,409
You came back earlier than I thought.

553
00:45:04,577 --> 00:45:06,454
I thought you'd be another hour.

554
00:45:08,206 --> 00:45:09,040
Let's go.

555
00:45:09,666 --> 00:45:11,334
There's a gift I want from you.

556
00:45:18,925 --> 00:45:22,595
Mi-do the weirdo, Mi-do the dork.

557
00:45:26,057 --> 00:45:26,933
Come on, smile.

558
00:45:28,852 --> 00:45:30,895
It's our last time together.
At least smile.

559
00:45:36,359 --> 00:45:38,111
Like I always say,

560
00:45:39,279 --> 00:45:41,156
you don't look half bad when you smile.

561
00:45:48,163 --> 00:45:49,205
Aren't you hungry?

562
00:45:49,998 --> 00:45:51,458
You barely ate earlier.

563
00:45:51,583 --> 00:45:53,251
Just tell me what you want.

564
00:45:53,376 --> 00:45:54,544
I'll buy it and leave.

565
00:45:54,669 --> 00:45:56,379
Come on, it's our last day anyway.

566
00:45:56,504 --> 00:45:59,340
-Stay with me until midnight, Mi-do!
-Hey!

567
00:46:10,393 --> 00:46:11,519
Um…

568
00:46:11,644 --> 00:46:12,645
A balloon.

569
00:46:15,482 --> 00:46:18,526
The dinosaur balloon
you gave me when we first met.

570
00:46:20,987 --> 00:46:23,072
I want one just like that.

571
00:46:25,867 --> 00:46:27,452
That balloon was actually…

572
00:46:29,579 --> 00:46:31,831
the first gift I ever got.

573
00:46:35,502 --> 00:46:39,339
So when I lost it, I was really sad.

574
00:46:50,225 --> 00:46:51,851
That was over 20 years ago.

575
00:46:51,976 --> 00:46:54,020
They wouldn't have the same one.

576
00:46:54,145 --> 00:46:55,146
Are you serious?

577
00:46:55,271 --> 00:46:57,774
Who would sell
those old-fashioned balloons these days?

578
00:47:33,893 --> 00:47:35,103
Wow, smell the ocean.

579
00:47:35,228 --> 00:47:36,854
We're at the beach! Jump in!

580
00:47:38,565 --> 00:47:40,024
-Jump in. He did.
-No, you!

581
00:47:40,149 --> 00:47:41,526
No, rock-paper-scissors.

582
00:47:42,860 --> 00:47:44,862
-Rock, paper, scissors!
-Shoot!

583
00:47:45,655 --> 00:47:47,949
-Rock, paper, scissors, shoot!
-Shoot!

584
00:47:48,074 --> 00:47:49,117
Oh, no.

585
00:47:49,242 --> 00:47:50,451
-No, no.
-Come on.

586
00:47:50,577 --> 00:47:51,494
You okay?

587
00:47:52,203 --> 00:47:54,372
Are you okay? Thank you.

588
00:47:54,497 --> 00:47:55,999
-Be careful.
-Thank you.

589
00:47:56,124 --> 00:47:58,710
Say thank you, okay?

590
00:47:59,961 --> 00:48:02,839
Excuse me, could you take our picture?

591
00:48:02,964 --> 00:48:03,923
Sure.

592
00:48:04,048 --> 00:48:05,216
-Visiting?
-Yes.

593
00:48:05,341 --> 00:48:07,051
-Wow, thank you.
-Get closer.

594
00:48:07,927 --> 00:48:09,012
One, two, three.

595
00:48:10,138 --> 00:48:11,973
-Guys, jump on three.
-Okay.

596
00:48:12,098 --> 00:48:13,433
-Get ready.
-Wait.

597
00:48:13,558 --> 00:48:14,976
Two, three!

598
00:48:16,936 --> 00:48:17,937
Did you get it?

599
00:48:18,813 --> 00:48:20,148
-Was it a selfie?
-Not so great.

600
00:48:20,273 --> 00:48:22,442
-Thank you.
-Thanks.

601
00:48:22,567 --> 00:48:23,651
Have fun, guys.

602
00:48:29,991 --> 00:48:31,159
What are you…

603
00:48:33,995 --> 00:48:35,121
Hey!

604
00:48:35,246 --> 00:48:37,081
I'll buy you another one next year.

605
00:48:38,583 --> 00:48:40,293
We don't have to come to Gangneung.

606
00:48:40,418 --> 00:48:42,337
I'll just buy you one next year.

607
00:48:44,505 --> 00:48:47,508
You said you'd see
Yeong-do and Wan-do once a year.

608
00:48:48,801 --> 00:48:51,220
You don't have to
see me that often, so just…

609
00:48:51,929 --> 00:48:53,973
don't say today is the end

610
00:48:54,098 --> 00:48:56,184
or that you'll never see me again.

611
00:49:06,694 --> 00:49:08,446
Mi-do, you want to know a secret?

612
00:49:12,825 --> 00:49:13,868
Actually…

613
00:49:14,952 --> 00:49:16,829
I won't see Yeong-do and Wan-do.

614
00:49:18,831 --> 00:49:21,668
They need some time.

615
00:49:24,045 --> 00:49:25,630
So I'm just waiting for them.

616
00:49:28,049 --> 00:49:29,717
Every three years,

617
00:49:31,260 --> 00:49:32,387
then every five years.

618
00:49:34,347 --> 00:49:35,890
That's how I'll fade away.

619
00:49:38,142 --> 00:49:39,310
Namgung.

620
00:49:40,144 --> 00:49:42,313
Don't do this. Why are you doing this?

621
00:49:42,438 --> 00:49:43,523
Mi-do.

622
00:49:47,402 --> 00:49:49,445
Why did you give me that balloon?

623
00:49:53,282 --> 00:49:54,951
I've always wondered that.

624
00:49:59,622 --> 00:50:01,290
Why did you give it to me?

625
00:50:03,668 --> 00:50:05,795
Did you also feel sorry for me back then?

626
00:50:13,636 --> 00:50:14,929
I'm not telling you.

627
00:50:16,139 --> 00:50:18,433
You said you'd never see me again.

628
00:50:18,558 --> 00:50:20,518
So I'm never telling you either.

629
00:51:26,417 --> 00:51:27,919
Someone fell in!

630
00:51:28,044 --> 00:51:30,588
Help! Someone's drowning!

631
00:52:00,076 --> 00:52:00,952
No!

632
00:52:17,134 --> 00:52:18,094
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

633
00:52:18,219 --> 00:52:20,096
-Thank you so much.
-Thank you.

634
00:52:20,221 --> 00:52:21,389
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

635
00:52:21,514 --> 00:52:22,640
-You okay?
-Yes.

636
00:52:28,813 --> 00:52:31,190
-Hey.
-Don't be mad.

637
00:52:32,900 --> 00:52:34,819
You can't be mad. It's our last time.

638
00:52:39,156 --> 00:52:40,700
Namgung.

639
00:52:42,827 --> 00:52:44,161
You're wrong.

640
00:52:47,415 --> 00:52:49,000
How is this a curse?

641
00:52:52,169 --> 00:52:54,797
I was scared the whole time I was running,

642
00:52:56,424 --> 00:52:58,426
but I couldn't stop.

643
00:53:02,513 --> 00:53:03,806
You were too, right?

644
00:53:08,519 --> 00:53:10,563
My dad would've felt the same.

645
00:53:28,831 --> 00:53:30,374
It wasn't a curse.

646
00:53:32,251 --> 00:53:33,836
It was a miracle.

647
00:53:37,757 --> 00:53:39,759
It was a miracle that we met.

648
00:53:44,055 --> 00:53:45,556
Still, Namgung,

649
00:53:47,183 --> 00:53:48,851
if your survival…

650
00:53:50,770 --> 00:53:52,229
ever makes you regret it

651
00:53:53,064 --> 00:53:54,690
and blame yourself,

652
00:53:56,067 --> 00:53:58,778
and feels like a curse,

653
00:54:01,072 --> 00:54:03,699
remember that kid you and I saved.

654
00:54:07,161 --> 00:54:11,916
That alone makes meeting each other
more than a blessing.

655
00:54:27,348 --> 00:54:29,100
I wanted you to be happy.

656
00:54:32,853 --> 00:54:34,981
When I gave you that balloon,

657
00:54:36,941 --> 00:54:40,611
I just thought, "I hope that little boy

658
00:54:41,654 --> 00:54:42,863
will be happy."

659
00:54:46,325 --> 00:54:47,618
I was happy.

660
00:54:49,996 --> 00:54:50,871
Mi-do.

661
00:54:51,998 --> 00:54:53,457
Knowing you

662
00:54:54,458 --> 00:54:57,128
made me so breathtakingly happy.

663
00:54:58,170 --> 00:55:00,589
You're the one who taught me

664
00:55:00,715 --> 00:55:02,174
that life could be this happy.

665
00:55:03,175 --> 00:55:06,262
That's what kept me alive.
That's how I carried on.

666
00:55:07,179 --> 00:55:09,390
I was able to try my hardest to live.

667
00:55:19,483 --> 00:55:22,028
What about you, Mi-do?

668
00:55:23,029 --> 00:55:24,822
Were you happy with me?

669
00:55:36,459 --> 00:55:39,545
It was worth giving my all.

670
00:55:42,006 --> 00:55:45,134
That's how happy I was, Namgung.

671
00:56:04,153 --> 00:56:08,324
Excuse me, this was caught
on a shop sign over there.

672
00:56:12,078 --> 00:56:13,996
Thank you so much.

673
00:57:09,927 --> 00:57:11,554
About eight minutes left.

674
00:57:14,223 --> 00:57:17,434
If you have any last questions, ask away.

675
00:57:18,227 --> 00:57:20,521
What did you do with Angela at the motel?

676
00:57:26,610 --> 00:57:30,197
Forget it. Don't tell me.
I don't want to know.

677
00:57:38,914 --> 00:57:40,166
Mi-do.

678
00:57:42,668 --> 00:57:44,170
Yes?

679
00:57:46,088 --> 00:57:47,965
Lee Mi-do.

680
00:57:49,091 --> 00:57:50,509
Yes?

681
00:57:53,721 --> 00:57:55,931
Can you please say my name?

682
00:58:08,110 --> 00:58:09,612
Namgung Ho.

683
00:58:13,866 --> 00:58:17,036
Namgung Ho, the happy pushover.

684
00:59:08,837 --> 00:59:10,214
I totally got ripped off.

685
00:59:10,339 --> 00:59:11,382
AFTER SPRING COMES WINTER

686
00:59:11,507 --> 00:59:13,133
A hundred thousand won each.

687
00:59:14,093 --> 00:59:16,512
Not even a discount, those bastards.

688
00:59:17,221 --> 00:59:20,307
Quitting movies is one thing,

689
00:59:21,058 --> 00:59:24,561
but that doesn't erase your past.

690
00:59:26,313 --> 00:59:30,526
All that time you spent working hard
belongs to you.

691
00:59:30,651 --> 00:59:31,819
So…

692
00:59:35,739 --> 00:59:37,992
don't tear it up or ruin it.

693
00:59:38,701 --> 00:59:40,244
Cherish it.

694
00:59:41,704 --> 00:59:44,540
Both the movie and Hoya.

695
00:59:45,916 --> 00:59:47,334
Cherish them.

696
00:59:58,679 --> 01:00:01,598
What? Why are you here?

697
01:00:01,724 --> 01:00:03,017
I came to see Mi-do.

698
01:00:03,142 --> 01:00:04,685
I'm dating Mi-do.

699
01:00:04,810 --> 01:00:07,980
Hey, I won't be your brother-in-law.

700
01:00:08,689 --> 01:00:10,316
-Get lost.
-Don't flatter yourself.

701
01:00:10,441 --> 01:00:12,943
I don't want you
as a brother-in-law either.

702
01:00:13,068 --> 01:00:16,655
Look at that idiot. He's back again.

703
01:00:16,780 --> 01:00:18,574
Go ahead and talk down to me, pal.

704
01:00:18,699 --> 01:00:19,575
What, "pal"?

705
01:00:19,700 --> 01:00:20,534
"Pal"?

706
01:00:21,535 --> 01:00:22,786
What did you say? "Pal"?

707
01:00:22,911 --> 01:00:24,997
I'm older! Even my face looks older.

708
01:00:25,122 --> 01:00:26,707
Whoa, let go of my collar!

709
01:00:26,832 --> 01:00:28,042
Oh, fighting back?

710
01:00:28,167 --> 01:00:29,209
Hitting me again?

711
01:00:59,782 --> 01:01:02,117
Namgung found something of yours
while packing.

712
01:01:02,242 --> 01:01:05,162
He left it by your door. Did you see it?

713
01:01:20,135 --> 01:01:23,138
Namgung, you and I

714
01:01:23,847 --> 01:01:26,058
gave each other a seed.

715
01:01:31,772 --> 01:01:32,773
Namgung.

716
01:01:33,816 --> 01:01:37,486
You've received seeds from so many.

717
01:01:38,946 --> 01:01:41,407
Your biological father
who left you at birth.

718
01:01:42,533 --> 01:01:44,868
My dad, who died saving you.

719
01:01:45,744 --> 01:01:48,205
Aunt Hwa-young,
who broke you again and again.

720
01:01:48,956 --> 01:01:51,125
Art, once your whole world.

721
01:01:51,959 --> 01:01:54,169
Ssuk, the cat I was jealous of.

722
01:01:55,087 --> 01:01:57,089
Sol, who was so much like you.

723
01:01:57,923 --> 01:02:01,552
So many gave you seeds and left.

724
01:02:16,316 --> 01:02:20,279
VOL. 8

725
01:02:20,404 --> 01:02:25,159
Namgung, you gave me such deep love

726
01:02:25,784 --> 01:02:29,079
and looked at the world with such warmth

727
01:02:31,498 --> 01:02:33,709
because you didn't neglect those seeds.

728
01:02:34,543 --> 01:02:37,671
You made them grow strong
and helped them bloom.

729
01:02:41,175 --> 01:02:42,843
So, Namgung.

730
01:02:44,011 --> 01:02:45,095
Just like you,

731
01:02:46,346 --> 01:02:49,391
I'm going to nurture
this seed you gave me.

732
01:02:50,851 --> 01:02:54,897
Without neglecting it,
without letting it fester and rot,

733
01:02:55,939 --> 01:02:57,941
without trampling and killing it,

734
01:02:59,026 --> 01:03:02,279
I'll nurture it warmly
with the love you taught me.

735
01:03:03,197 --> 01:03:05,699
And I will make sure it blooms.

736
01:03:22,132 --> 01:03:23,133
Namgung.

737
01:03:24,051 --> 01:03:26,845
Instead of the first snow,
let's wait for spring now.

738
01:03:28,847 --> 01:03:32,643
The spring when the seed you gave me
blooms inside me.

739
01:03:34,186 --> 01:03:37,814
The spring when the seed I gave you
blooms inside you.

740
01:03:40,192 --> 01:03:42,194
And let's love that spring.

741
01:03:43,779 --> 01:03:44,821
Forever.

742
01:05:19,333 --> 01:05:20,500
THANK YOU TO KIM YOON-HYE
FOR HER SPECIAL APPEARANCE

743
01:05:51,239 --> 01:05:54,201
THANK YOU FOR WATCHING
A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

744
01:05:57,287 --> 01:05:59,247
Subtitle translation by Cayle Kim
